Date: Thu, 6 Jan 94 10:25:02 CST
From: eder@hsvaic.hv.boeing.com (Dani Eder)
Subject: Extropially Correct Welfare

On the issue of parents educating children:

It seems quite simple to me.  If the first thing you own is
yourself (your body), then the fruits of that body you also own.
So, you own your children.  The children need to buy their self-
ownership from their parents.  Some parents (probably most) will
freely give this ownership away.  Some may set a price to
recover their costs (I invested 12 years raising you - Now
I want half your earnings for the next twelve years to pay me back).
Some may not give away anything - but retain ownership of
their children until they die, then willing their ownership
to their kids at that time.  Some may sell the ownership to
others.

People who are owned by others, and want the maximum productivity
out of their property, will want to properly motivate their
property - I suspect a reasonable sale price and a reasonable way
to accumulate the sales price are good inducements to work hard.

Dani Eder

